THIRD-PARTY SOFTWARE

The ovrin core module has no external dependencies (docs/rules.md §4.1), so
depending on ovrin itself brings in nothing but ovrin. Everything below arrives
only if you import the optional module that carries it: each adapter is its own
module with its own go.mod, precisely so that this list is something you opt
into a line at a time (docs/rules.md §4.2).

Ovrin's dependency licence policy permits only Apache-2.0, BSD-2-Clause,
BSD-3-Clause, MIT, ISC and MPL-2.0; AGPL and GPL are excluded
(docs/adr/0025-licence-policy.md).

The versions named below are the ones in each module's go.mod. That file and
its go.sum are authoritative for what you actually build against; this file is
a human-readable summary of them and is revised when they change. A module
listed as having no third-party dependencies has none at all — no direct
requirement and no indirect one.

  .                  the core        no third-party dependencies
  ocr/azure                          no third-party dependencies
  ocr/google                         no third-party dependencies
  ocr/textract                       no third-party dependencies
  model/skyl                         attributions below
  ocr/tesseract                      attributions below
  otel                               attributions below
  render/pdfium                      attributions below
  examples/receipt                   attributions below

The three cloud OCR adapters carry nothing because they speak to their
providers over net/http from the standard library rather than through a vendor
SDK. That is the point of the seam, not an accident of it
(docs/adr/0009-ocr-seam.md).


